267
00:16:18,680 --> 00:16:22,386
Oh, it seems there's been some
remodeling done here in the city

268
00:16:22,840 --> 00:16:24,840
Might this be your work?

269
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:29,940
No, ma 'am I arrived here just a moment
ago I haven't a clue what happened

270
00:16:30,480 --> 00:16:31,310
Oh?

271
00:16:32,400 --> 00:16:34,929
If you can spare but
a moment of your time?

272
00:16:36,080 --> 00:16:39,237
There are some things I would
like to speak to you about today.

273
00:16:39,320 --> 00:16:40,340
It's important.

274
00:16:48,140 --> 00:16:50,860
You're not going to
leave my crew, are you?

275
00:16:57,940 --> 00:16:59,820
I have faith in Straw Hat,

276
00:17:00,100 --> 00:17:03,512
and I am confident that he
will change this world someday.

277
00:17:04,060 --> 00:17:05,500
He is young, I know,

278
00:17:05,760 --> 00:17:08,237
but I do not believe that
any of the four emperors

279
00:17:08,320 --> 00:17:11,144
have what it takes to
become king of these seas.

280
00:17:11,260 --> 00:17:13,380
But Straw Hat Luffy isn't like them.

281
00:17:13,680 --> 00:17:15,445
That boy is something special.

282
00:17:20,480 --> 00:17:24,009
Therefore, I've decided that I
want to lend him my strength.

283
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:31,757
I'm so...

284
00:17:31,840 --> 00:17:34,380
I'm so weak!

285
00:17:35,240 --> 00:17:37,660
More than that, I want to join his crew.

286
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:43,317
I want to ride upon his ship, and I
want to dedicate my life to his journey.

287
00:17:43,400 --> 00:17:44,760
In the end,

288
00:17:44,980 --> 00:17:50,040
I believe the world he creates will be a
world where fishmen are truly free at last.

289
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:57,828
We all know plenty about Luffy,
Jinbei, if we're being frank.

290
00:17:57,960 --> 00:18:00,937
You've been going on and on
about him for the past two years.

291
00:18:01,020 --> 00:18:03,357
I don't disagree with
your decision, though.

292
00:18:03,440 --> 00:18:06,911
If you want to join Luffy that
much, then maybe you should.

293
00:18:07,580 --> 00:18:08,960
Oh, I'm so sorry.

294
00:18:09,240 --> 00:18:11,460
Did I talk about him that much?

295
00:18:13,840 --> 00:18:15,300
Just go, Jean-Babe.

296
00:18:15,540 --> 00:18:16,460
We don't mind.

297
00:18:19,300 --> 00:18:20,340
Are you certain?

298
00:18:22,800 --> 00:18:24,657
We can't even complain, Captain.

299
00:18:24,740 --> 00:18:26,337
We totally get how you feel.

300
00:18:26,420 --> 00:18:30,220
And besides, you quit your job
in the Neptune Army to help us.

301
00:18:30,360 --> 00:18:31,877
That's why you're a pirate, right?

302
00:18:31,960 --> 00:18:34,477
We were just a bunch of
slaves from Marie Joie,

303
00:18:34,560 --> 00:18:37,357
but you were willing to do
anything to fight by our side.

304
00:18:37,440 --> 00:18:39,117
Even when you joined the Warlords,

305
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:42,671
you only did it to advance the
status of us fishmen, right?

306
00:18:42,900 --> 00:18:44,140
Same with big mom.

307
00:18:44,500 --> 00:18:49,537
That's why you got all buddy-buddy with
her to protect the Ryugu kingdom You throw

308
00:18:49,620 --> 00:18:54,057
the name of an emperor around and even the
real tough guys will get off your back!

309
00:18:54,140 --> 00:18:56,037
Everything you've done
has been to help our

310
00:18:56,120 --> 00:18:58,532
people you turned our whole lives around.

311
00:18:59,800 --> 00:19:01,580
You've done enough for us.

312
00:19:01,880 --> 00:19:03,000
It's all right

313
00:19:05,980 --> 00:19:09,820
Yeah, Captain now is your
time break out and be free

314
00:19:11,920 --> 00:19:13,391
That's what you gotta do!

315
00:19:13,540 --> 00:19:15,380
We'll be fine without you.

316
00:19:15,580 --> 00:19:17,300
Don't underestimate us.

317
00:19:17,580 --> 00:19:19,497
Time to start living for yourself.

318
00:19:19,580 --> 00:19:20,940
Going where you want.

319
00:19:37,640 --> 00:19:38,960
Thank you.

320
00:19:39,780 --> 00:19:40,740
Thank you.

321
00:19:51,820 --> 00:19:52,880
But I don't know.

322
00:19:53,100 --> 00:19:55,017
Even if we're cool with
the captain leaving,

323
00:19:55,100 --> 00:19:57,877
I have a feeling Big Mom ain't
gonna be too happy about this.

324
00:19:57,960 --> 00:20:00,697
If she gets mad, then all
he can do is run away.

325
00:20:00,780 --> 00:20:02,040
Maybe better to swim.

326
00:20:03,060 --> 00:20:03,890
Huh?

327
00:20:03,973 --> 00:20:05,837
But then what's Aladdin supposed to do?

328
00:20:05,920 --> 00:20:06,750
Huh?

329
00:20:07,740 --> 00:20:11,837
He's a member of Big Mom's family
since he's married to Lady Prawlane.

330
00:20:11,920 --> 00:20:13,700
Now, what was that?

331
00:20:15,280 --> 00:20:18,340
You aren't worried about
little old me, are you?

332
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:20,380
Ah, it's her!

333
00:20:21,340 --> 00:20:22,740
Sha, sha, sha.

334
00:20:24,820 --> 00:20:29,320
Were you naughty boys talking
about me behind my back? Oh, crap.

335
00:20:29,580 --> 00:20:30,540
Did she hear us?

336
00:20:30,860 --> 00:20:34,320
You're hiding something from
me, my darling little hubby.

337
00:20:35,500 --> 00:20:36,637
Aladdin, fuss up.

338
00:20:36,720 --> 00:20:38,900
If Mama got angry at your crew,

339
00:20:39,080 --> 00:20:41,137
were you gonna scurry off
in the middle of the night?

340
00:20:41,220 --> 00:20:42,337
and leave me behind?

341
00:20:42,420 --> 00:20:44,657
No, uh, I would ask you first, my dear.

342
00:20:44,740 --> 00:20:46,916
What makes you think you need to ask?

343
00:20:47,400 --> 00:20:50,320
I choose you over Mama
any day of the week.

344
00:20:50,460 --> 00:20:53,048
If you have to leave,
then take me with you.

345
00:20:53,320 --> 00:20:54,940
Oh, so passionate!

346
00:20:57,260 --> 00:20:58,660
Forgive me, Waratsumi.

347
00:20:58,900 --> 00:21:01,782
I just brought you here,
and I'm already leaving.

348
00:21:02,340 --> 00:21:03,960
Aw, it's fine.

349
00:21:04,260 --> 00:21:07,200
I love being with these
guys, so I'm still happy.

350
00:21:10,200 --> 00:21:12,180
Well, what say you, Praline?

351
00:21:12,420 --> 00:21:13,780
Will Mama forgive me?

352
00:21:14,660 --> 00:21:17,497
Or rather, will she forgive
us if I try to leave?

353
00:21:17,580 --> 00:21:18,480
Good question.

354
00:21:18,920 --> 00:21:20,720
Others have tried it before.

355
00:21:21,320 --> 00:21:26,360
I don't know exactly how the negotiations
went, but I know that they're dead.

356
00:21:50,140 --> 00:21:52,360
Oh, Commander Mascotto!

357
00:21:52,640 --> 00:21:55,640
He just wanted to protect
us and now he's dead!

358
00:21:55,960 --> 00:21:57,460
No, this can't be true!

359
00:21:57,680 --> 00:21:59,562
You've got to get off, Mascotto!

360
00:21:59,840 --> 00:22:01,280
Please don't die!

361
00:22:08,840 --> 00:22:10,800
We've finally decided to show up.

362
00:22:17,600 --> 00:22:20,000
Hurry and take him away. Yes, ma 'am.

363
00:22:20,520 --> 00:22:21,402
Out of the way.

364
00:22:32,460 --> 00:22:33,680
Listen up, damn it.

365
00:22:34,280 --> 00:22:35,720
Every single second.

366
00:22:35,960 --> 00:22:37,540
You understand me?

367
00:22:56,280 --> 00:22:57,860
Hell if I know!

368
00:22:58,400 --> 00:23:03,940
But if you cross mama, this is what's gonna
happen to you even if you're her child.

369
00:23:14,340 --> 00:23:17,720
Hmm, so you really want
to leave me, Jinbae?

370
00:23:20,560 --> 00:23:22,000
Don't go, boss!

371
00:23:22,200 --> 00:23:23,117
Why would you leave?

372
00:23:23,200 --> 00:23:25,460
Don't you love us anymore? Shut up!

373
00:23:32,560 --> 00:23:34,597
Don't ask someone why they're leaving.

374
00:23:34,680 --> 00:23:36,856
Do you know how pathetic that sounds?

375
00:23:37,080 --> 00:23:38,860
What does it matter, anyway?

376
00:23:42,280 --> 00:23:46,820
Jinbei is a pirate, and we
always live the way we choose.

377
00:23:53,200 --> 00:23:56,680
That said, having a
pledge of loyalty reneged

378
00:23:57,340 --> 00:23:59,140
brings shame to a leader.

379
00:24:02,500 --> 00:24:07,380
Jinbei, I'm losing a very
powerful asset here. Namely, you.

380
00:24:08,060 --> 00:24:10,277
Well, perhaps...

381
00:24:10,360 --> 00:24:11,900
Perhaps, you say?

382
00:24:12,200 --> 00:24:14,800
If I'm losing something, you should, too.

383
00:24:15,240 --> 00:24:17,860
That means you have to pay the price.

384
00:24:20,840 --> 00:24:22,860
Ma-ma-ma-ma-ma!

385
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:26,440
Bring me the roulette!

386
00:24:27,180 --> 00:24:28,010
What?!

387
00:24:43,080 --> 00:24:45,120
Now spin it!

388
00:24:50,540 --> 00:24:53,960
Come on, let's see what
you lose, shall we?

389
00:24:54,880 --> 00:24:57,160
I can't wait!

390
00:25:02,680 --> 00:25:06,798
Meanwhile, Luffy and company continue
their trek to Whole Cake Island.

391
00:25:09,920 --> 00:25:10,750
Yummy!

392
00:25:12,720 --> 00:25:15,597
I'm afraid we're not making
much progress, are we?

393
00:25:15,680 --> 00:25:16,510
No kidding.

394
00:25:16,593 --> 00:25:19,280
You want to start a
campfire and take a nap?

395
00:25:19,440 --> 00:25:21,497
And get attacked by those ants again?

396
00:25:21,580 --> 00:25:22,540
No thank you.

397
00:25:23,160 --> 00:25:26,757
At night time, the syrupy
seas get cold and solidify.

398
00:25:26,840 --> 00:25:29,980
When the sun rises, it'll
begin to flow again.

399
00:25:30,300 --> 00:25:32,771
Tell us these things beforehand next time.

400
00:25:34,760 --> 00:25:38,977
Just melt this batch of starch syrup, and
hopefully we'll be on our way in no time.

401
00:25:39,060 --> 00:25:39,890
You got it.

402
00:25:40,860 --> 00:25:41,690
Keep going.

403
00:25:41,773 --> 00:25:43,380
We're not exactly safe here.

404
00:25:43,640 --> 00:25:45,699
I only put those sea ants to sleep.

405
00:25:45,800 --> 00:25:47,937
They're gonna be mad when they wake up.

406
00:25:48,020 --> 00:25:49,160
Oh, undoubtedly so.

407
00:25:52,460 --> 00:25:54,397
Those ants can eat an entire ship.

408
00:25:54,480 --> 00:25:56,177
I'd know since it happened to mine.

409
00:25:56,260 --> 00:25:58,340
No way! Hey, Pedro!

410
00:25:58,760 --> 00:26:01,348
You said you came here
once before, but why?

411
00:26:01,720 --> 00:26:02,940
Pedro and Peckhams?

412
00:26:03,140 --> 00:26:05,737
They used to be pirates
and traveled here together.

413
00:26:05,820 --> 00:26:06,650
Really?

414
00:26:06,733 --> 00:26:08,032
You should have told me!

415
00:26:08,920 --> 00:26:10,380
I was so naive.

416
00:26:11,140 --> 00:26:15,375
I thought of myself as a grand explorer,
but I soon became a wanted man.

417
00:26:15,560 --> 00:26:18,736
At any rate, I only accompanied
Peckhams half the way.

418
00:26:20,460 --> 00:26:22,460
Please keep this story between us.

419
00:26:23,340 --> 00:26:25,720
I wanted to help Master Catviper.

420
00:26:26,260 --> 00:26:29,060
So I was scouring these
waters for poneglyphs.

421
00:26:30,900 --> 00:26:36,200
But when I trespassed in Big Mom's
territory it became my last voyage.

422
00:26:39,840 --> 00:26:43,560
I faced a devastating defeat here.

423
00:26:51,380 --> 00:26:53,145
I don't talk about this often.

424
00:26:54,520 --> 00:26:55,780
Pedro I never knew.

425
00:27:04,740 --> 00:27:07,540
You have bad memories
but you still came back.

426
00:27:08,060 --> 00:27:13,300
If my experience helps then it will all
be worth it if you Karoo can rescue Sanji.

427
00:27:16,460 --> 00:27:20,460
Besides this might be a chance to
rectify my failure from last time.

428
00:27:21,940 --> 00:27:24,297
I heard that Yugara
went to the whale tree.

429
00:27:24,380 --> 00:27:27,937
And that our kings showed
Yugara the road poneglyph there.

430
00:27:28,020 --> 00:27:30,920
That was quite a surprise.

431
00:27:32,040 --> 00:27:33,360
I'll put it this way.

432
00:27:33,940 --> 00:27:36,977
No one outside the Kozuki
clan has seen that place.

433
00:27:37,060 --> 00:27:39,960
In nearly 26 years or so.

434
00:27:41,180 --> 00:27:44,317
Specifically since they showed
it to Goldie Roger and his crew.

435
00:27:44,400 --> 00:27:46,640
The king of the pirates was there?

436
00:27:47,040 --> 00:27:51,100
Yes And after that, he sailed to
Laugh Tale and earned that title.

437
00:27:53,820 --> 00:27:55,040
In other words,

438
00:27:55,360 --> 00:27:58,037
Duke Dogstorm and Master
Catviper think Yugara

439
00:27:58,120 --> 00:28:00,767
have the same qualities
that Roger possessed.

440
00:28:03,180 --> 00:28:05,877
They showed Yugara the
Road Poneglyph because

441
00:28:05,960 --> 00:28:07,997
they believed you might need it someday.

442
00:28:08,080 --> 00:28:10,668
What is your plan after
Yugara defeat Kaido?

443
00:28:10,980 --> 00:28:12,500
That's too far ahead.

444
00:28:12,840 --> 00:28:14,397
I haven't even thought about it.

445
00:28:14,480 --> 00:28:19,068
If you, Karoo, want to see this through,
you'll need Big Mom's Road Poneglyph.

446
00:28:19,620 --> 00:28:21,973
Since we're this far into her territory,

447
00:28:22,120 --> 00:28:25,940
it might be your best, if not
only, opportunity to find it.

448
00:28:26,120 --> 00:28:28,360
So in addition to taking back Sanji,

449
00:28:28,600 --> 00:28:32,071
I believe we should steal Big
Mom's Road Poneglyph as well.

450
00:28:34,100 --> 00:28:36,460
But can we do that?

451
00:28:38,140 --> 00:28:40,964
But rescuing Sanji might
be hard enough already.

452
00:28:44,480 --> 00:28:47,068
Robin did ask me about
it, but I don't know.

453
00:28:47,220 --> 00:28:50,000
Maybe after we save Sanji? I understand.

454
00:28:50,680 --> 00:28:53,386
I'll get the Poneglyph,
you, Karoo, get Sanji.

455
00:28:54,040 --> 00:28:55,099
That satisfactory?

456
00:28:58,140 --> 00:29:01,846
When we reach the island, can
you, Karoo, buy me a little time?

457
00:29:02,120 --> 00:29:04,760
I swear I won't fail again. Hold on.

458
00:29:04,960 --> 00:29:05,842
We'll help you.

459
00:29:06,000 --> 00:29:08,177
I mean, you're doing
this for us, after all.

460
00:29:08,260 --> 00:29:09,090
I'm fine.

461
00:29:09,240 --> 00:29:11,593
It'll be hard enough to keep Sanji safe.

462
00:29:12,120 --> 00:29:14,179
Rescuing him is just the beginning.

463
00:29:19,200 --> 00:29:20,340
I get it.

464
00:29:20,680 --> 00:29:21,860
Well, good luck.

465
00:29:23,260 --> 00:29:24,480
Good. It's settled.

466
00:29:24,940 --> 00:29:26,764
Shouldn't we talk this through?

467
00:29:27,620 --> 00:29:28,840
Sometimes I wonder,

468
00:29:29,080 --> 00:29:33,080
do things work out for Luffy because
he was born under a lucky star?

469
00:29:33,380 --> 00:29:34,674
What was that, Brooke?

470
00:29:35,580 --> 00:29:36,410
Nothing.

471
00:29:36,493 --> 00:29:37,340
I'm lucky myself.

472
00:29:37,960 --> 00:29:39,548
What are you talking about?

473
00:29:39,700 --> 00:29:40,530
Don't be weird.

474
00:29:53,780 --> 00:29:54,610
Ah!

475
00:29:54,693 --> 00:29:56,920
The ants woke up! No!

476
00:30:02,480 --> 00:30:03,310
Ah!

477
00:30:03,393 --> 00:30:04,720
Protect the Snow!

478
00:30:15,880 --> 00:30:17,940
Hey, you guys!

479
00:30:18,360 --> 00:30:19,440
Wake up!

480
00:30:22,320 --> 00:30:23,540
Yoho?

481
00:30:24,280 --> 00:30:25,840
What is it?

482
00:30:37,580 --> 00:30:38,410
Look!

483
00:30:51,260 --> 00:30:53,017
So we finally made it!

484
00:30:53,100 --> 00:30:54,020
Oh ho ho ho!

485
00:30:59,560 --> 00:31:01,840
That's one fancy looking island!

486
00:31:03,120 --> 00:31:06,240
So this is the kind of
place an emperor lives!

487
00:31:07,420 --> 00:31:09,260
That's a big cake!

488
00:31:11,740 --> 00:31:14,360
The tallest cake there
is actually a castle.

489
00:31:14,660 --> 00:31:17,800
Naturally, that's where
Big Mom lives. Oh, wow!

490
00:31:18,220 --> 00:31:21,460
Nami, should I keep steering
us straight? Uh-huh.

491
00:31:21,740 --> 00:31:23,269
We're headed to that cape.

492
00:31:23,520 --> 00:31:25,402
It's a hole in the security net.

493
00:31:26,120 --> 00:31:26,950
I see.

494
00:31:27,033 --> 00:31:28,972
Everything's gone just like Pudding said.

495
00:31:29,300 --> 00:31:30,130
Yeah.

496
00:31:30,213 --> 00:31:32,777
I wish there was some way to
thank her for all her help.

497
00:31:32,860 --> 00:31:36,637
If we hadn't met her, I don't know
if we would have made it this far.

498
00:31:36,720 --> 00:31:38,120
That is so true.

499
00:31:39,840 --> 00:31:41,080
Look!

500
00:31:41,440 --> 00:31:42,860
Somebody's on the shore!

501
00:31:49,940 --> 00:31:51,560
No way!

502
00:31:51,920 --> 00:31:53,180
It's Sanji!

503
00:31:54,480 --> 00:31:55,310
Hey!

504
00:31:55,393 --> 00:31:56,320
Sanji!
